styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="95">Here’s a clear comparative table mapping <strong data-start="41" data-end="67">Hinrichs et al. (2025)</strong> to your <strong data-start="76" data-end="94">RSVP framework</strong>:</p>
<hr data-start="97" data-end="100">
<h3 data-start="102" data-end="176">Comparative Table: <em data-start="125" data-end="160">Geometric Hyperscanning of Affect</em> vs. RSVP Theory</h3>
<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="178" data-end="2962" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="178" data-end="289"><tr data-start="178" data-end="289"><th data-start="178" data-end="207" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="180" data-end="206">Hinrichs et al. (2025)</strong></th><th data-start="207" data-end="254" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="209" data-end="253">RSVP (Relativistic Scalar-Vector Plenum)</strong></th><th data-start="254" data-end="289" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="256" data-end="287">Connection / Interpretation</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="400" data-end="2962"><tr data-start="400" data-end="759"><td data-start="400" data-end="524" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="402" data-end="432">Dyadic generative manifold</strong> – the minimal unit of analysis is the coupled system of two agents in recursive inference.</td><td data-start="524" data-end="636" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="526" data-end="536">Plenum</strong> – global scalar–vector–entropy field where local patches (Φ, 𝒗, S) glue into a coherent manifold.</td><td data-start="636" data-end="759" data-col-size="lg">Both emphasize <strong data-start="653" data-end="674">relational wholes</strong> (dyads or patches) as the true generative unit, not isolated individuals or cells.</td></tr><tr data-start="760" data-end="1072"><td data-start="760" data-end="870" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="762" data-end="811">Valence as identity-relevant prediction error</strong> – affect emerges from mismatches in self-model coherence.</td><td data-start="870" data-end="990" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="872" data-end="892">Entropic descent</strong> – gravitational, cognitive, and semantic processes emerge from entropic smoothing of mismatches.</td><td data-start="990" data-end="1072" data-col-size="lg">Both use <strong data-start="1001" data-end="1029">deviation from coherence</strong> as the fundamental driver of adaptation.</td></tr><tr data-start="1073" data-end="1379"><td data-start="1073" data-end="1172" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="1075" data-end="1094">Temporal aiming</strong> – prospective vs. retrospective appraisal, fast vs. slow affective dynamics.</td><td data-start="1172" data-end="1269" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="1174" data-end="1203">Recursive causality loops</strong> – RSVP’s forward–backward entropic flows and trajectory buffers.</td><td data-start="1269" data-end="1379" data-col-size="lg">Temporal nonlocality in both: affect aims across past and future; RSVP fields carry memory and projection.</td></tr><tr data-start="1380" data-end="1713"><td data-start="1380" data-end="1490" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="1382" data-end="1417">Affective rupture–repair cycles</strong> – misalignment raises free energy; repair restores narrative coherence.</td><td data-start="1490" data-end="1619" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="1492" data-end="1521">Entropy tears &amp; smoothing</strong> – breakdowns of plenum coherence (entropy tears) followed by lamphron–lamphrodyne reintegration.</td><td data-start="1619" data-end="1713" data-col-size="lg">Both describe <strong data-start="1635" data-end="1656">phase transitions</strong> as breakdown and re-coherence of the generative field.</td></tr><tr data-start="1714" data-end="2044"><td data-start="1714" data-end="1817" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="1716" data-end="1756">Forman-Ricci curvature entropy (FRc)</strong> – captures reconfiguration of inter-brain network topology.</td><td data-start="1817" data-end="1940" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="1819" data-end="1881">Topological invariants (homotopy colimits, derived stacks)</strong> – formalize gluing of local patches into a global plenum.</td><td data-start="1940" data-end="2044" data-col-size="lg">FRc ≈ RSVP’s topological entropy metrics; both detect <strong data-start="1996" data-end="2041">geometric markers of coherence or rupture</strong>.</td></tr><tr data-start="2045" data-end="2352"><td data-start="2045" data-end="2141" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="2047" data-end="2063">Sociomarkers</strong> – curvature-based indices of rupture, repair, and attunement for psychiatry.</td><td data-start="2141" data-end="2252" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="2143" data-end="2168">Consciousness metrics</strong> – field coherence, coupling strength, thermodynamic complexity for RSVP cognition.</td><td data-start="2252" data-end="2352" data-col-size="lg">Both propose <strong data-start="2267" data-end="2291">quantitative markers</strong> of relational/mental states based on geometry and entropy.</td></tr><tr data-start="2353" data-end="2673"><td data-start="2353" data-end="2464" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="2355" data-end="2385">Second-person neuroscience</strong> – interaction itself is the explanandum; “I–Thou” exchange as coupled system.</td><td data-start="2464" data-end="2577" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="2466" data-end="2495">RSVP’s entropic semantics</strong> – meaning emerges not in isolation but through entangled fields of Φ, 𝒗, and S.</td><td data-start="2577" data-end="2673" data-col-size="lg">Both reject observer-only models; emphasize <strong data-start="2623" data-end="2653">co-construction of meaning</strong> in shared fields.</td></tr><tr data-start="2674" data-end="2962"><td data-start="2674" data-end="2770" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="2676" data-end="2717">Policy selection modulated by valence</strong> – affect guides actions toward restoring coherence.</td><td data-start="2770" data-end="2872" data-col-size="lg"><strong data-start="2772" data-end="2818">Constraint relaxation via entropic descent</strong> – vector flows reconfigure fields to reduce tension.</td><td data-start="2872" data-end="2962" data-col-size="lg">Both make <strong data-start="2884" data-end="2928">affect/entropy the regulator of dynamics</strong>, shaping adaptive trajectories.</td></tr></tbody></table><div class="sticky h-0 select-none end-(--thread-content-margin) self-end"><div class="absolute end-0 flex items-end" style="height: 48.7031px;"><span class="" data-state="closed"><button aria-label="Copy table" class="hover:bg-token-bg-tertiary text-token-text-secondary my-1 rounded-sm p-1 transition-opacity group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:pointer-events-none group-[:not(:hover):not(:focus-within)]:opacity-0"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 8.33399C3.28478 8.49198 3.22795 8.70352 3.19727 9.0791C3.16595 9.46259 3.16504 9.95611 3.16504 10.667V13.5C3.16504 14.211 3.16593 14.7044 3.19727 15.0879C3.22797 15.4636 3.28473 15.675 3.36524 15.833L3.43555 15.959C3.61186 16.2466 3.86474 16.4807 4.16699 16.6348L4.29688 16.6914C4.44063 16.7428 4.63025 16.7797 4.91211 16.8027C5.29563 16.8341 5.78896 16.835 6.5 16.835H9.33301C10.0439 16.835 10.5374 16.8341 10.9209 16.8027C11.2965 16.772 11.508 16.7152 11.666 16.6348L11.793 16.5645C12.0804 16.3881 12.3148 16.1351 12.4688 15.833L12.5244 15.7031C12.5759 15.5594 12.6137 15.3698 12.6367 15.0879C12.6681 14.7044 12.668 14.211 12.668 13.5V10.667ZM13.998 12.665C14.4528 12.6634 14.8011 12.6602 15.0879 12.6367C15.4635 12.606 15.675 12.5492 15.833 12.4688L15.959 12.3975C16.2466 12.2211 16.4808 11.9682 16.6348 11.666L16.6914 11.5361C16.7428 11.3924 16.7797 11.2026 16.8027