.1667em;"></span><span class="mop">lo<span style="margin-right: 0.01389em;">g</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.9484em;"><span style="top: -2.3987em; margin-left: -0.0738em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.03148em;">k</span><span class="mord mtight">ℓ</span></span></span></span><span style="top: -3.1809em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathrm mtight">joint</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3013em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mord"><span class="delimsizing size2">)</span></span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="6990" data-end="7352">Thus, <em data-start="6996" data-end="7012">theory of mind</em> is <strong data-start="7016" data-end="7062">intentionality extended beyond the blanket</strong>: the same manifold-comparison calculus is applied to external, inferred manifolds <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="script">M</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>j</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal M^j_\ell\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.2439em; vertical-align: -0.3013em;"></span><span class="mopen">{</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal">M</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.9426em;"><span style="top: -2.3987em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">ℓ</span></span></span><span style="top: -3.1809em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3013em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">}</span></span></span></span>, with the coupling kernel <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal K</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.01445em;">K</span></span></span></span> mediating entanglement. Constructive cross-boundary interference formalizes <strong data-start="7288" data-end="7302">attunement</strong>; destructive interference formalizes <strong data-start="7340" data-end="7351">rupture</strong>.</p>
<hr data-start="7354" data-end="7357">
<h2 data-start="7359" data-end="7385">Notes on implementation</h2>
<ul data-start="7386" data-end="8046">
<li data-start="7386" data-end="7613">
