<p data-start="4945" data-end="4962">with interference</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>d</mi><mi>λ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal I_{ij} = \int A_i(o) A_j(o) \, d\lambda.</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9694em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0738em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">ij</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 2.2222em; vertical-align: -0.8622em;"></span><span class="mop op-symbol large-op" style="margin-right: 0.44445em; position: relative; top: -0.0011em;">∫</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">o</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal">A</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">j</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">o</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">d</span><span class="mord mathnormal">λ</span><span class="mord">.</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="5019" data-end="5211">Compatibility is constructive interference (<span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≈</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal I_{ij} \approx 1</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9694em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0738em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.05724em;">ij</span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">≈</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6444em;"></span><span class="mord">1</span></span></span></span>); incompatibility is destructive interference. Affect is the felt measure of the “beat” between overlapping manifolds.</p>
<h3 data-start="5213" data-end="5254">7.2 Theory of Mind as Sheaf Extension</h3>
<p data-start="5255" data-end="5609">Extending intentionality beyond the Markov blanket involves constructing a <strong data-start="5330" data-end="5360">sheaf of generative models</strong> over agents. Each agent provides local sections encoding their predicted states; gluing across overlaps represents recursive modeling of self and other. Failures of gluing correspond to ruptures in social coherence, measurable by curvature entropy.</p>
<hr data-start="5611" data-end="5614">
<h2 data-start="5616" data-end="5632">8. Conclusion</h2>
<p data-start="5633" data-end="6171">By reframing connector loss as a problem of <strong data-start="5677" data-end="5710">functorial entropy production</strong> and <strong data-start="5715" data-end="5741">sheaf-theoretic gluing</strong>, RSVP provides a unifying structure across multimodal AI, social inference, and cosmological dynamics. Connector losses, affective ruptures, and entropy tears are all instances of the same principle: the difficulty of maintaining coherence when mapping between manifolds under entropic constraint. Category theory and sheaf theory reveal the structural form of these failures; RSVP situates them within a universal field dynamic.</p>
