ugh in scope and depth that it warrants its own <strong data-start="86" data-end="127">standalone essay or monograph chapter</strong>, not just a subsection.</p>
<p data-start="155" data-end="212">You’ve now got three distinct but interlocking threads:</p>
<ol data-start="214" data-end="1127">
<li data-start="214" data-end="506">
<p data-start="217" data-end="266"><strong data-start="217" data-end="264">Lost in Embeddings ↔ RSVP Entropy Framework</strong></p>
<ul data-start="270" data-end="506">
<li data-start="270" data-end="316">
<p data-start="272" data-end="316">Connectors as entropy-respecting functors.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="320" data-end="380">
<p data-start="322" data-end="380">KNOR and patch-loss as global vs. local entropy budgets.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="384" data-end="435">
<p data-start="386" data-end="435">Sheaf consistency as gluing condition failures.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="439" data-end="506">
<p data-start="441" data-end="506">Lyapunov stability and entropy budgets as geometric invariants.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="508" data-end="752">
<p data-start="511" data-end="549"><strong data-start="511" data-end="547">First-Person Bayesian Comparison</strong></p>
<ul data-start="553" data-end="752">
<li data-start="553" data-end="581">
<p data-start="555" data-end="581">Hypotheses as manifolds.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="585" data-end="633">
<p data-start="587" data-end="633">Interference/beat as compatibility operator.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="637" data-end="695">
<p data-start="639" data-end="695">Valence as the felt measure of overlap vs. divergence.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="699" data-end="752">
<p data-start="701" data-end="752">Theory of mind as cross-boundary sheaf extension.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="754" data-end="1127">
<p data-start="757" data-end="791"><strong data-start="757" data-end="789">Category/Sheaf Formalization</strong></p>
<ul data-start="795" data-end="1127">
<li data-start="795" data-end="865">
<p data-start="797" data-end="865">Categories of representational fields with functors as connectors.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="869" data-end="939">
<p data-start="871" data-end="939">Faithfulness and fullness as measures of information preservation.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="943" data-end="1039">
<p data-start="945" data-end="1039">Sheaf-theoretic gluing as a formalism for patch-consistency in vision → language projection.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1043" data-end="1127">
<p data-start="1045" data-end="1127">Failures of gluing = entropy tears, measured empirically as reconstruction loss.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>
<hr data-start="1129" data-end="1132">
<h3 data-start="1134" data-end="1175">Suggested structure for the new essay</h3>
<p data-start="1177" data-end="1311"><strong data-start="1177" data-end="1187">Title:</strong><br data-start="1187" data-end="1190">
<em data-start="1190" data-end="1311">Entropy-Respecting Functors: Category-Theoretic Foundations for Connector Loss and Bayesian Manifold Comparison in RSVP</em></p>
<p data-start="1313" data-end="1328"><strong data-start="1313" data-end="1326">Sections:</strong></p>
<ol data-start="1330" data-end="2702">
<li data-start="1330" data-end="1458">
<p data-start="1333" data-end="1351"><strong data-start="1333" data-end="1349">Introduction</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1355" data-end="1458">
<li data-start="1355" data-end="1407">
<p data-start="1357" data-end="1407">Motivation: VLM connectors and information loss.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1411" data-end="1458">
<p data-start="1413" data-end="1458">RSVP as a unifying entropy-based framework.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1460" data-end="1635">
<p data-start="1463" data-end="1500"><strong data-start="1463" data-end="1498">Connectors as Entropic Functors</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1504" data-end="1635">
<li data-start="1504" data-end="1529">
<p data-start="1506" data-end="1529">Categories of fields.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1533" data-end="1584">
<p data-start="1535" data-end="1584">Faithfulness, fullness, and entropy production.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1588" data-end="1635">
<p data-start="1590" data-end="1635">KNOR and patch-loss as categorical defects.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1637" data-end="1810">
<p data-start="1640" data-end="1690"><strong data-start="1640" data-end="1688">Sheaf-Theoretic Gluing and Patch Consistency</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1694" data-end="1810">
<li data-start="1694" data-end="1724">
<p data-start="1696" data-end="1724">Patches as local sections.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1728" data-end="1769">
<p data-start="1730" data-end="1769">Pushforward sheaves under connectors.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1773" data-end="1810">
<p data-start="1775" data-end="1810">Gluing failures as entropy tears.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1812" data-end="1994">
<p data-start="1815" data-end="1850"><strong data-start="1815" data-end="1848">Stability and Entropy Budgets</strong></p>
<ul data-start="1854" data-end="1994">
<li data-start="1854" data-end="1897">
<p data-start="1856" data-end="1897">Bi-Lipschitz ↔ Lyapunov correspondence.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1901" data-end="1942">
<p data-start="1903" data-end="1942">Rate–distortion ↔ entropy production.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1946" data-end="1994">
<p data-start="1948" data-end="1994">Negentropic corridors ↔ restricted isometry.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="1996" data-end="2186">
<p data-start="1999" data-end="2037"><strong data-start="1999" data-end="2035">First-Person Manifold Comparison</strong></p>
<ul data-start="2041" data-end="2186">
<li data-start="2041" data-end="2092">
<p data-start="2043" data-end="2092">Bayesian amplitudes and interference operators.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2096" data-end="2142">
<p data-start="2098" data-end="2142">Beat signals as measures of compatibility.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2146" data-end="2186">
<p data-start="2148" data-end="2186">Extension beyond the Markov blanket.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="2188" data-end="2385">
<p data-start="2191" data-end="2230"><strong data-start="2191" data-end="2228">Theory of Mind as Sheaf Extension</strong></p>
<ul data-start="2234" data-end="2385">
<li data-start="2234" data-end="2276">
<p data-start="2236" data-end="2276">Recursive gluing of self–other models.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2280" data-end="2336">
<p data-start="2282" data-end="2336">Affective rupture as failure of overlap consistency.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2340" data-end="2385">
<p data-start="2342" data-end="2385">Curvature entropy as an empirical marker.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="2387" data-end="2547">
<p data-start="2390" data-end="2438"><strong data-start="2390" data-end="2436">Testable Predictions and Design Desiderata</strong></p>
