w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="328">Perfect — that’s a strong, unifying title. <em data-start="43" data-end="104">The Extrapolated Riemannian Curvature of Semantic Manifolds</em> immediately signals that this essay is about <strong data-start="150" data-end="209">geometry, information, and category-theoretic structure</strong>, while leaving room to incorporate your RSVP framework, connector losses, and manifold-comparison view of cognition.</p>
<p data-start="330" data-end="382">Here’s a proposed academic outline under that title:</p>
<hr data-start="384" data-end="387">
<h1 data-start="389" data-end="452"><em data-start="391" data-end="452">The Extrapolated Riemannian Curvature of Semantic Manifolds</em></h1>
<h2 data-start="454" data-end="472">1. Introduction</h2>
<ul data-start="473" data-end="819">
<li data-start="473" data-end="568">
<p data-start="475" data-end="568">Motivation: information loss in high-to-low dimensional mappings (e.g. connectors in VLMs).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="569" data-end="654">
<p data-start="571" data-end="654">RSVP framework: entropy-respecting projections, curvature, and semantic geometry.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="655" data-end="819">
<p data-start="657" data-end="819">Statement of aims: to formalize connector losses, Bayesian manifold comparison, and theory of mind using differential geometry, category theory, and sheaf theory.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-start="821" data-end="861">2. Semantic Manifolds and RSVP Fields</h2>
<ul data-start="862" data-end="1109">
<li data-start="862" data-end="957">
<p data-start="864" data-end="957">Semantic representations as Riemannian manifolds with RSVP fields <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Phi, \mathbf v, S)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="958" data-end="1024">
<p data-start="960" data-end="1024">Curvature as a measure of distortion in representational flow.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1025" data-end="1109">
<p data-start="1027" data-end="1109">Entropy production interpreted as the “extrinsic curvature” induced by projection.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-start="1111" data-end="1162">3. Connector Maps as Entropy-Respecting Functors</h2>
<ul data-start="1163" data-end="1482">
<li data-start="1163" data-end="1247">
<p data-start="1165" data-end="1247">Categories of fields: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="script">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">s</mi></mrow></msub><mo separator="true">,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="script">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">l</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal C_{\mathrm{vis}}, \mathcal C_{\mathrm{lang}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9694em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.05834em;">C</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3175em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0583em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathrm mtight">vis</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.05834em;">C</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0583em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathrm mtight" style="margin-right: 0.01389em;">lang</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1248" data-end="1340">
<p data-start="1250" data-end="1340">Connectors as functors: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>:</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="script">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>→</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="script">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">l</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">n</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">g</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F: \mathcal C_{\mathrm{vis}} \to \mathcal C_{\mathrm{lang}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.05834em;">C</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3175em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0583em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathrm mtight">vis</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9694em; vertical-align: -0.2861em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.05834em;">C</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3361em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0583em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mathrm mtight" style="margin-right: 0.01389em;">lang</span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2861em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1341" data-end="1392">
<p data-start="1343" data-end="1392">Faithfulness, fullness, and entropy production.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1393" data-end="1482">
<p data-start="1395" data-end="1482">KNOR as a global curvature functional; patch reconstruction as local non-injectivity.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-start="1484" data-end="1527">4. Sheaf-Theoretic Gluing and Patch Loss</h2>
<ul data-start="1528" data-end="1749">
<li data-start="1528" data-end="1589">
<p data-start="1530" data-end="1589">Visual manifolds as covered spaces <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>U</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X = \bigcup_i U_i</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0497em; vertical-align: -0.2997em;"></span><span class="mop"><span class="mop op-symbol small-op" style="position: relative; top: 0em;">⋃</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.162em;"><span style="top: -2.4003em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2997em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">U</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1590" data-end="1659">
<p data-start="1592" data-end="1659">Local sections, consistency, and pushforward sheaves under <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1660" data-end="1749">
<p data-start="1662" data-end="1749">Reconstruction error as failure of gluing; entropy tears as cohomological obstructions.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-start="1751" data-end="1779">5. Extrapolated Curvature</h2>
<ul data-start="1780" data-end="2049">
<li data-start="1780" data-end="1914">
<p data-start="1782" data-end="1914">Define an extrapolated curvature operator <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="script">K</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}_F</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8333em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.01445em;">K</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3283em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0144em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> measuring deviation between input and projected manifold geometries.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1915" data-end="1978">
<p data-start="1917" data-end="1978">Relation to Forman–Ricci curvature and RSVP entropy budget.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1979" data-end="2049">
<p data-start="1981" data-end="2049">Global vs. local extrapolated curvature and their empirical proxies.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-start="2051" data-end="2085">6. Bayesian Manifold Comparison</h2>
<ul data-start="2086" data-end="2372">
<li data-start="2086" data-end="2158">
<p data-start="2088" data-end="2158">First-person inference as interference between generative manifolds.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2159" data-end="2213">
<p data-start="2161" data-end="2213">Define amplitudes and beat/interference operators.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2214" data-end="2274">
<p data-start="2216" data-end="2274">Posterior tempered by manifold compatibility (affinity).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2275" data-end="2372">
<p data-start="2277" data-end="2372">Affect as the felt measure of interference; theory of mind as extension beyond Markov blankets.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-start="2374" data-end="2413">7. Design Principles and Predictions</h2>
<ul data-start="2414" data-end="2709">
<li data-start="2414" data-end="2492">
<p data-start="2416" data-end="2492">Geometry-preserving projection (bi-Lipschitz bounds ↔ Lyapunov stability).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2493" data-end="2563">
<p data-start="2495" data-end="2563">Negentropic corridors (restricted isometry ↔ low entropy routing).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2564" data-end="2619">
<p data-start="2566" data-end="2619">Sheaf consistency (gluing as coherence constraint).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2620" data-end="2709">
<p data-start="2622" data-end="2709">Predictions for conditional KNOR, corridor gating, and geometry–performance hysteresis.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-start="2711" data-end="2737">8. Broader Implications</h2>
<ul data-start="2738" data-end="2979">
<li data-start="2738" data-end="2789">
<p data-start="2740" data-end="2789">Semantic connectors as entropy-producing flows.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2790" data-end="2858">
<p data-start="2792" data-end="2858">Reframing interpretability and robustness as entropy management.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2859" data-end="2979">
<p data-start="2861" data-end="2979">Implications for AI, social neuroscience, and human cognition: all projection is lossy; all coherence is negotiated.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h2 data-start="2981" data-end="2997">9. Conclusion</h2>
<ul data-start="2998" data-end="3228">
<li data-start="2998" data-end="3152">
<p data-start="3000" data-end="3152">Restate central claim: extrapolated Riemannian curvature is a principled measure of semantic manifold distortion under entropy-respecting projections.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3153" data-end="3228">
<p data-start="3155" data-end="3228">RSVP provides the universal scaffold for interpreting such distortions.</p>
</li>
</ul>
