rst:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="263">The problem is that your <code data-start="25" data-end="33">tikzcd</code> diagrams are too wide for the text block. By default, <code data-start="88" data-end="96">tikzcd</code> will happily let labels sprawl out, and with long labels like <code data-start="159" data-end="224">\llbracket \mathrm{Pop}(\mathrm{Sphere}(x{:}A.\,t),u)\rrbracket</code>, you’ll end up exceeding <code data-start="250" data-end="262">\textwidth</code>.</p>
<p data-start="265" data-end="309">Here are some practical fixes you can apply:</p>
<hr data-start="311" data-end="314">
<h3 data-start="316" data-end="371">1. Use <code data-start="327" data-end="339">column sep</code> and <code data-start="344" data-end="353">row sep</code> more aggressively</h3>
<p data-start="372" data-end="462">You’ve already tried <code data-start="393" data-end="411">column sep=small</code>. You can reduce it further or set a uniform scale:</p>
