We outline the main constructions and proof obligations. Full proofs follow by
routine inductions on typing and reduction derivations, plus standard descent
arguments for sheaves and information-metric preservation.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Setup (categories and interpretation).}
Let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Syn}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> be the syntactic category of well-typed SPC terms with
objects </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span> A)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and morphisms generated by typing derivations and
operational reductions. Let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{StatMan}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> be the category of statistical
manifolds with Fisher metrics </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>g</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>F</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and information-preserving smooth maps.
The interpretation </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>:</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Syn}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{StatMan}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is
defined by:
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{itemize}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Objects: </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\vdash</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a statistical manifold 
  built in a presheaf topos </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span> E=[</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Sphere}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{op},</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Set}]</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
  equipped with (i) cartesian closed structure (</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Rightarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{ev}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>),
  (ii) symmetric monoidal structure (</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> for concurrency),
  (iii) a probability monad </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> (Giry/Jacobs--Fritz).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\item</span></span><span> Morphisms: typing derivations map to CCC/SMC structure; operational
  reductions map to their semantic counterparts (evaluation, tensor,
  mixing) via the adequacy diagrams (below).
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{itemize}

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Lemma 1 (Sphere/Pop diagrammatic adequacy).}
For any </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\beta</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-redex, the diagram
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tikzcd}[column sep=small]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[r,"{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> f </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\pi</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>2</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span>}"]
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[d,swap,"{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{oper.}}"]
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> A</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Rightarrow</span></span><span> B </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[r,"</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{ev}"]
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> B </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[rr,swap,"{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Pop}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Sphere}(x{:}A.</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\,</span></span><span>t),u)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>}"]
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> B </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tikzcd}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
commutes.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Sketch.} CCC coherence: evaluation is natural in both arguments; the
operational rule for application corresponds to </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{ev}</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\circ</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\langle</span></span><span> -, -</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rangle</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
Induction on typing of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>t,u</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> plus functoriality of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Lemma 2 (Merge adequacy).}
For parallel composition,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tikzcd}[column sep=small]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> u </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[rr,"</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cong</span></span><span>"]
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[d,swap,"{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{oper. flattening}}"]
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> u </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[d,"{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{tensor}}"] </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Merge}(t,u) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[rr,equal]
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Merge}(t,u) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tikzcd}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
commutes.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Sketch.} </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Sem}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a symmetric monoidal category; operational
flattening is interpreted by the monoidal product. Use naturality of the
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> constraint and the SMC coherence theorems.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Lemma 3 (Choice adequacy).}
For probabilistic branching,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tikzcd}[column sep=small]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[r,"{(p,t,u)}"]
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[d,swap,"{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{sampling}}"]
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> [0,1]</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\times</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>2
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[r,"</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{mix}"]
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Gamma</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[rr,swap,"{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Choice}(p,t,u)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>}"]
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> A </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tikzcd}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
commutes.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Sketch.} By the Eilenberg–Moore algebra laws for the distribution monad,
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{mix}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is bilinear and respects substitution; the operational sampling
rule corresponds to the monadic bind on </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Lemma 4 (Independent Channels Lemma).}
For independent merges,
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\[</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\begin</span></span><span>{tikzcd}[column sep=small]
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\textstyle</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\prod</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}(O)
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[r,"</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span>"]
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[d,swap,"{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{oper. Merge}}"]
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}(O</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>n)
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[r,"{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{anyDoom}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\*</span></span><span>}"]
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}(O) </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\\</span></span><span>
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}(O)
  </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\ar</span></span><span>[rr,equal]
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">&amp;</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}(O)
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\end</span></span><span>{tikzcd}
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\]</span></span><span>
commutes.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Sketch.} Product measures in </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> correspond to monoidal
products; </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{anyDoom}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\*</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> pushes forward along the disjunctive map
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>O</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>n</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> O</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>. Fubini/Tonelli and monad algebra laws yield equality.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Lemma 5 (Presheaf </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\Rightarrow</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> sheaf via descent).}
Let </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\{</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\}</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> be the local semantics on a cover
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span> U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> of the syntactic manifold. Then </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> satisfies
the sheaf gluing condition.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Sketch.} Each adequacy diagram is a local compatibility condition on
overlaps </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>i</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cap</span></span><span> U</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>j</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> (naturality of </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{ev}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{mix}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>).
These give a </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\v</span></span><span>{C}ech </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>1</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-cocycle valued in isomorphisms; coherence (from CCC/SMC
laws and monad laws) trivializes the cocycle, so </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\check</span></span><span>{H}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>1(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathcal</span></span><span> U,</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathrm</span></span><span>{Iso})=0</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
hence unique gluing.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Lemma 6 (Fisher metric preservation).}
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> - </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> preserves Fisher information up to isometry:
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>g</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>F(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cong</span></span><span> g</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>F(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> t' </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> whenever </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>t</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\to</span></span><span> t'</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Sketch.} Endow </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{Dist}(-)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> with the Fisher metric; </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{mix}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>,
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{ev}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> are smooth maps that are
(i) </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{LC}}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>-compatible (preserve the Levi–Civita connection) and
(ii) likelihood-sufficient (no loss of sufficient statistics). Hence they are
information non-increasing; the adequacy diagrams force equality. Naturality
yields a family of local isometries that glue by Lemma~5.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Lemma 7 (Curvature invariance).}
The Riemann tensor </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>F</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is a natural invariant along reductions:
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>F(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> t </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\cong</span></span><span> R</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>F(</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\llbracket</span></span><span> t' </span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\rrbracket</span></span><span>)</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\emph</span></span><span>{Sketch.} Curvature is determined by </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>g</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>F</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> and </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\nabla</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">^</span></span><span>{</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\!</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\text</span></span><span>{LC}}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
By Lemma~6, </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>g</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">_</span></span><span>F</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span> is preserved up to isometry, and by functoriality of
</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{ev}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\otimes</span></span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{mix}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>, the induced connections coincide on
overlaps; thus the pulled-back curvature tensors agree and glue globally.

</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\paragraph</span></span><span>{Conclusion.}
Lemmas~1–4 establish diagrammatic adequacy; Lemma~5 gives the sheaf condition;
Lemmas~6–7 yield Fisher and curvature preservation. Therefore the four clauses
of the Adequacy Theorem hold, and SPC is interpreted as a Fisher-preserving,
curvature-preserving sheaf functor into </span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\mathsf</span></span><span>{StatMan}</span><span><span class="hljs-built_in">$</span></span><span>.
</span><span><span class="hljs-keyword">\qed</span></span><span>
</span></span></code></div></div></pre>
