6.01057 5.53708 6.00551 6.00391 6.00391C6.00551 5.53708 6.01057 5.14051 6.03809 4.80371C6.0755 4.34588 6.15483 3.94012 6.34668 3.56348L6.46875 3.34473C6.77282 2.84912 7.20856 2.44514 7.72949 2.17969L7.87207 2.11328C8.20855 1.96886 8.56979 1.90385 8.9707 1.87109C9.42091 1.83432 9.978 1.83496 10.667 1.83496H13.5C14.1891 1.83496 14.746 1.83431 15.1963 1.87109C15.6541 1.90851 16.0599 1.98788 16.4365 2.17969L16.6553 2.30176C17.151 2.60585 17.5548 3.04244 17.8203 3.56348L17.8867 3.70606C18.031 4.04235 18.0962 4.40306 18.1289 4.80371C18.1657 5.25395 18.165 5.81091 18.165 6.5V9.33301Z"></path></svg>Copy code</button></div></div></div><div class="overflow-y-auto p-4" dir="ltr"><code class="whitespace-pre! language-pseudo"><span>PROCEDURE SmallWorldRewiringSweep(N, K, p_grid, curvature, entropy_estimator) -&gt; control
    control = {"p": [], "HRC": [], "quantiles": []}
    FOR p IN p_grid:
        G = WattsStrogatzWeighted(N, K, p)   # base ring + rewiring + random weights
        curv = {}
        IF curvature["FRC"]: curv_vals = FormanRicciCurvature(G, "degree")
        # (optionally ORC here)
        H = DifferentialEntropy(curv_vals, entropy_estimator)
        Q = Quantiles(curv_vals, [0.05, 0.5, 0.95])
        control["p"].append(p)
        control["HRC"].append(H)
        control["quantiles"].append(Q)
    END FOR
    RETURN control
END PROCEDURE
</span></code></div></div></pre>
<hr data-start="9545" data-end="9548">
<h2 data-start="9550" data-end="9586">Practical defaults (per modality)</h2>
<ul data-start="9588" data-end="9894">
<li data-start="9588" data-end="9709">
<p data-start="9590" data-end="9709">EEG: <code data-start="9595" data-end="9615">window_len_sec=2–4</code>, <code data-start="9617" data-end="9636">step_sec=0.25–0.5</code>, <code data-start="9638" data-end="9656">ibs_metric="PLV"</code> (band-limited), intra-brain <code data-start="9685" data-end="9690">kNN</code> scaffolds helpful.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="9710" data-end="9806">
<p data-start="9712" data-end="9806">fNIRS: <code data-start="9719" data-end="9740">window_len_sec=5–15</code>, <code data-start="9742" data-end="9761">ibs_metric="corr"</code> or coherence, downsampled; stronger pruning.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="9807" data-end="9894">
<p data-start="9809" data-end="9894">fMRI: <code data-start="9815" data-end="9837">window_len_sec=30–60</code> (blocks), coherence/corr; interpret as slow regime only.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="9896" data-end="9899">
<h2 data-start="9901" data-end="9920">Complexity notes</h2>
<ul data-start="9922" data-end="10224">
<li data-start="9922" data-end="10010">
<p data-start="9924" data-end="10010">FRC: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mi>E</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∣</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>deg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(|E| + \sum_i \deg(i)^2)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">E</span><span class="mord">∣</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">+</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.1138em; vertical-align: -0.2997em;"></span><span class="mop"><span class="mop op-symbol small-op" style="position: relative; top: 0em;">∑</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.162em;"><span style="top: -2.4003em; margin-left: 0em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2997em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mop">de<span style="margin-right: 0.01389em;">g</span></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">i</span><span class="mclose"><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8141em;"><span style="top: -3.063em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight">2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> (practically linear in edges with adjacency lists).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="10011" data-end="10118">
<p data-start="10013" data-end="10118">ORC: dominated by many small OT problems on neighborhoods; use Sinkhorn with small ε and sparse supports.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="10119" data-end="10224">
<p data-start="10121" data-end="10224">Entropy: KDE <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> for evaluation per x with grid; histogram trivial; kNN estimator <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n \log n)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mop">lo<span style="margin-right: 0.01389em;">g</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="10226" data-end="10229">
<h2 data-start="10231" data-end="10276">RSVP / adequacy mapping (optional signals)</h2>
<ul data-start="10278" data-end="10551">
<li data-start="10278" data-end="10352">
<p data-start="10280" data-end="10352"><strong data-start="10280" data-end="10291">Rupture</strong> if: sharp ↑ in <code data-start="10307" data-end="10312">HRC</code> AND drop in <code data-start="10325" data-end="10351">NegentropicCorridorScore</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="10353" data-end="10424">
<p data-start="10355" data-end="10424"><strong data-start="10355" data-end="10365">Repair</strong> if: <code data-start="10370" data-end="10375">HRC</code> returns toward baseline AND corridors re-emerge.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="10425" data-end="10551">
<p data-start="10427" data-end="10551"><strong data-start="10427" data-end="10450">Task-aware analysis</strong>: recompute graphs conditioned on behavioral epochs; compare <code data-start="10511" data-end="10516">HRC</code> and corridor scores per condition.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="10553" data-end="10556">
