wn prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="301">I set up a Jupyter-ready Python scaffold that builds time-varying interbrain graphs, computes Forman–Ricci curvature (and a toy Ollivier–Ricci), estimates curvature-distribution entropy, and flags phase transitions—plus a synthetic demo. It’s already executed above; you can scroll to re-run or tweak.</p>
<p data-start="303" data-end="319">What’s included:</p>
<ul data-start="320" data-end="762">
<li data-start="320" data-end="431">
<p data-start="322" data-end="431">Sliding-window graph construction with inter-brain PLV (or correlation) + optional intra-brain kNN scaffolds.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="432" data-end="526">
<p data-start="434" data-end="526">FRC implementation; optional toy ORC (small graphs; replace with Sinkhorn/EMD for real use).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="527" data-end="569">
<p data-start="529" data-end="569">Differential entropy (histogram or KDE).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="570" data-end="607">
<p data-start="572" data-end="607">Simple CUSUM change-point detector.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="608" data-end="701">
<p data-start="610" data-end="701">“Negentropic corridor” score heuristic (edges with high weight and non-negative curvature).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="702" data-end="762">
<p data-start="704" data-end="762">Synthetic regime-shift demo with a single matplotlib plot.</p>
</li>
</ul>
