ty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling"><p data-start="0" data-end="183">Right now all the squeeze is going into your last column, because the first four are <code data-start="85" data-end="88">l</code>/<code data-start="89" data-end="92">l</code>/<code data-start="93" data-end="96">l</code>/<code data-start="97" data-end="100">l</code> which get as much space as they need, leaving only whatever is left for the <code data-start="177" data-end="180">X</code>.</p>
<p data-start="185" data-end="335">You can rebalance the widths by forcing the first three or four columns to be <strong data-start="263" data-end="288">narrower fixed widths</strong>, and leave the last one flexible. For example:</p>
