<h2 data-start="3552" data-end="3585">5. The Limits of Formalization</h2>
<p data-start="3586" data-end="3621">We prove the <strong data-start="3599" data-end="3620">Absurdity Theorem</strong>:</p>
<p data-start="3623" data-end="3740"><strong data-start="3623" data-end="3635">Theorem.</strong> For any human phenomenon <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.08125em;">H</span></span></span></span>, there exists a sequence of mathematical structures <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{M_i\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">{</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.10903em;">M</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.3117em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.109em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">i</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">}</span></span></span></span> such that</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><munder><mrow><mi>lim</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mtext>Explanatory&nbsp;Power</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo separator="true">,</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><munder><mrow><mi>lim</mi><mo>⁡</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mtext>Satirical&nbsp;Value</mtext><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">.</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{i\to\infty} \text{Explanatory Power}(M_i) = 0,
