ased extension</strong>, so the humor-as-manifold-shift model ties directly into <strong data-start="102" data-end="121">RSVP (Φ, 𝒗, S)</strong> and hyperscanning-style curvature/entropy tracking.</p>
<hr data-start="177" data-end="180">
<h2 data-start="182" data-end="205">Conceptual Framing</h2>
<ul data-start="207" data-end="785">
<li data-start="207" data-end="291">
<p data-start="209" data-end="291"><strong data-start="209" data-end="241">Semantic manifolds as graphs</strong>: nodes = concepts, edges = semantic affinities.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="292" data-end="377">
<p data-start="294" data-end="377"><strong data-start="294" data-end="322">Curvature (Forman–Ricci)</strong>: measures local expansion/bridging of semantic flow.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="378" data-end="454">
<p data-start="380" data-end="454"><strong data-start="380" data-end="391">Entropy</strong>: distribution of edge weights (uncertainty in associations).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="455" data-end="785">
<p data-start="457" data-end="575"><strong data-start="457" data-end="466">Humor</strong>: arises when a <em data-start="482" data-end="495">frame shift</em> suddenly reconfigures the graph (e.g. one edge weight is flipped or rewired).</p>
<ul data-start="578" data-end="785">
<li data-start="578" data-end="623">
<p data-start="580" data-end="623"><strong data-start="580" data-end="589">Setup</strong>: stable graph with low entropy.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="626" data-end="707">
<p data-start="628" data-end="707"><strong data-start="628" data-end="641">Punchline</strong>: edge rewiring produces incongruity (negative curvature spike).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="710" data-end="785">
<p data-start="712" data-end="785"><strong data-start="712" data-end="726">Resolution</strong>: integration re-stabilizes curvature, releasing entropy.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="787" data-end="807">This matches RSVP:</p>
<ul data-start="808" data-end="999">
<li data-start="808" data-end="878">
<p data-start="810" data-end="878"><strong data-start="810" data-end="826">Φ (capacity)</strong> = number of coherent nodes in the semantic field.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="879" data-end="939">
<p data-start="881" data-end="939"><strong data-start="881" data-end="901">𝒗 (vector flow)</strong> = semantic trajectory across edges.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="940" data-end="999">
<p data-start="942" data-end="999"><strong data-start="942" data-end="957">S (entropy)</strong> = disorder in edge-weight distribution.</p>
</li>
</ul>
