n processes, aligned with the RSVP fields and with curvature/geometry interpretations:</p>
<hr data-start="164" data-end="167">
<p data-start="169" data-end="234">\section{Taxonomy of Emotions as Recursive Surprise Minimization}</p>
<p data-start="236" data-end="2326">\begin{table}[H]<br>
\centering<br>
\caption{Emotions as recursive inoculation operators $\mathcal{I}^d$, with corresponding curvature signatures and RSVP field modulations.}<br>
\label{tab:emotion-taxonomy}<br>
\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{@{}l l l l X@{}}<br>
\toprule<br>
\textbf{Emotion} &amp; \textbf{Recursion depth $d$} &amp; \textbf{Curvature mode} &amp; \textbf{RSVP modulation} &amp; \textbf{Formal description} \<br>
\midrule<br>
Surprise &amp; $d=0$ &amp; Local curvature spike $\kappa \gg 0$ &amp; $S \uparrow$ sharply &amp; Raw divergence between prior $\mu$ and observation $x$; unbuffered prediction error. \<br>
\addlinespace<br>
Fear &amp; $d=1$ &amp; Negative curvature corridor &amp; $\mathbf{v} \downarrow$, $S \uparrow$ &amp; Anticipatory minimization of high-cost surprises; inoculation against catastrophic outcomes. \<br>
\addlinespace<br>
Humor &amp; $d=1$ (frame-shift) &amp; Interference / beat pattern &amp; $\Phi \uparrow$ transiently &amp; Resolution of mismatched manifolds via local isometry; sudden entropy release as coherence restoration. \<br>
\addlinespace<br>
Guilt &amp; $d=2$ &amp; Contractive curvature &amp; $\mathbf{v}$ retroactive, $S$ suppressed &amp; Inoculation against counterfactual priors $\mu'$; constrains manifold trajectories toward repair. \<br>
\addlinespace<br>
Awe &amp; $d \to \infty$ (limit) &amp; Curvature singularity $\kappa \to -\infty$ &amp; $\Phi \uparrow \uparrow$, $S \uparrow$ &amp; Epistemic expansion of representational volume; restructuring under incompressible novelty. \<br>
\addlinespace<br>
Nostalgia &amp; $d=2$ retrocausal &amp; Temporal pullback &amp; $\mathbf{v}$ reversed, $S \downarrow$ &amp; Recursive inoculation against temporal surprise; aligns present $q(x_t)$ with past distributions $q(x_{t-k})$. \<br>
\addlinespace<br>
Joy &amp; $d=1$ &amp; Flattened curvature $\kappa \approx 0$ &amp; $\Phi \uparrow$, $S \downarrow$ &amp; Inoculation aligns expectation and outcome; minimal prediction error with positive reinforcement. \<br>
\addlinespace<br>
Grief &amp; $d=2$ but unsatisfiable &amp; Persistent negative curvature &amp; $\Phi \downarrow$, $S \uparrow$ chronic &amp; Failed inoculation: recursive attempts cannot resolve loss manifold, producing enduring curvature distortion. \<br>
\bottomrule<br>
\end{tabularx}<br>
\end{table}</p>
<hr data-start="2328" data-end="2331">
<p data-start="2333" data-end="2372">This gives a compact formal comparison:</p>
<ul data-start="2374" data-end="2701">
<li data-start="2374" data-end="2479">
<p data-start="2376" data-end="2479"><strong data-start="2376" data-end="2390">Column 1–2</strong> classify emotions by recursion depth (how many levels of anticipation are inoculated).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2480" data-end="2575">
<p data-start="2482" data-end="2575"><strong data-start="2482" data-end="2494">Column 3</strong> maps to curvature signatures (spikes, flattening, contraction, singularities).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2576" data-end="2642">
<p data-start="2578" data-end="2642"><strong data-start="2578" data-end="2590">Column 4</strong> shows RSVP modulation in $(\Phi, \mathbf{v}, S)$.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2643" data-end="2701">
<p data-start="2645" data-end="2701"><strong data-start="2645" data-end="2657">Column 5</strong> explains the mathematical interpretation.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2703" data-end="2706">
<p data-start="2708" data-end="2967" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to also <strong data-start="2734" data-end="2776">draw the category/sheaf correspondence</strong> (objects = affective manifolds, morphisms = inoculation operators, curvature shifts as natural transformations), so the taxonomy sits within a categorical framework rather than just a table?</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.3