s push the taxonomy into categorical and sheaf-theoretic language so it integrates directly with your RSVP framework.</p>
<hr data-start="135" data-end="138">
<p data-start="140" data-end="196">\section{Categorical and Sheaf-Theoretic Correspondence}</p>
<p data-start="198" data-end="232">\subsection{Objects and Morphisms}</p>
<p data-start="234" data-end="301">We treat each affective state as a \emph{semantic manifold} object:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">E</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi mathvariant="bold">v</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E} = (X,g,\Phi,\mathbf{v},S)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.08944em;">E</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.07847em;">X</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">g</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord">Φ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathbf" style="margin-right: 0.01597em;">v</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="346" data-end="494">where $X$ is the underlying state space, $g$ the induced Riemannian metric, $\Phi$ scalar capacity, $\mathbf{v}$ vector flows, and $S$ entropy flux.</p>
<p data-start="496" data-end="585">Recursive self-inoculation is formalized as a morphism in the category $\mathsf{Affect}$:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="script">I</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant="script">E</mi><mo>→</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="script">E</mi><mo mathvariant="normal" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">′</mo></msup><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}^d : \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{E}',</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8991em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.07382em;">I</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8991em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">d</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.08944em;">E</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.9963em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.08944em;">E</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8019em;"><span style="top: -3.113em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mtight"><span class="mord mtight">′</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="638" data-end="843">where $d$ denotes recursion depth. Composition $\mathcal{I}^d \circ \mathcal{I}^{d'}$ corresponds to layered anticipation (e.g. guilt as a second-order inoculation against surprise about one’s own agency).</p>
<p data-start="845" data-end="880">\subsection{Sheaf-Theoretic Gluing}</p>
<p data-start="882" data-end="1174">Let ${\mathcal{U}_i}$ be an open cover of the cognitive manifold (perceptual frames, memory traces, social priors).<br data-start="999" data-end="1002">
Emotions arise when local inoculation operators $\mathcal{I}^d_i$ defined on each patch fail or succeed to glue consistently on overlaps $\mathcal{U}_i \cap \mathcal{U}_j$.</p>
<ul data-start="1176" data-end="1348">
<li data-start="1176" data-end="1222">
<p data-start="1178" data-end="1222">Successful gluing: coherence (joy, humor).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1223" data-end="1293">
<p data-start="1225" data-end="1293">Partial gluing with high entropy boundaries: ambivalence, anxiety.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1294" data-end="1348">
<p data-start="1296" data-end="1348">Failure to glue (no global section): grief, despair.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="1350" data-end="1462">Thus curvature entropy $H_{RC}$ functions as an obstruction measure in the Čech cohomology of affective sheaves.</p>
<p data-start="1464" data-end="1500">\subsection{Natural Transformations}</p>
<p data-start="1502" data-end="1545">We formalize affective dynamics as functors</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">C</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">o</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">n</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">t</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">e</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">x</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">t</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">A</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">f</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">f</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">e</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">c</mi><mi mathvariant="sans-serif">t</mi></mrow><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F,G : \mathsf{Context} \to \mathsf{Affect},</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mpunct">,</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathsf">Context</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8889em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathsf">Affect</span></span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1596" data-end="1675">mapping situational contexts to emotional manifolds.<br data-start="1648" data-end="1651">
A natural transformation</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta : F \Rightarrow G</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">η</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">⇒</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="1705" data-end="1849">represents the curvature-induced shift of emotional framing (e.g. awe as $\eta$ from a low-dimensional to a high-dimensional embedding functor).</p>
<p data-start="1851" data-end="1880">\subsection{RSVP Integration}</p>
<p data-start="1882" data-end="1981">The RSVP fields $(\Phi, \mathbf{v}, S)$ provide the semantic payload of these categorical mappings:</p>
<ul data-start="1983" data-end="2190">
<li data-start="1983" data-end="2054">
<p data-start="1985" data-end="2054">$\Phi$ tracked under adjunctions (capacity preserved or amplified).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2055" data-end="2125">
<p data-start="2057" data-end="2125">$\mathbf{v}$ transported functorially as vector flow of inference.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2126" data-end="2190">
<p data-start="2128" data-end="2190">$S$ bounded by curvature distortion as a naturality condition.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="2192" data-end="2201">Formally:</p>
<span class="katex-display"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>→</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mspace width="1em"></mspace><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>κ</mi><mo separator="true">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_x : F(x) \to G(x) \quad \text{s.t.} \quad S(F(x)) - S(G(x)) = \Delta \kappa,</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.625em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.03588em;">η</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.1514em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0359em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">x</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">:</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">→</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">)</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord text"><span class="mord">s.t.</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 1em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.13889em;">F</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">))</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span><span class="mbin">−</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2222em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05764em;">S</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">G</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">x</span><span class="mclose">))</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.8778em; vertical-align: -0.1944em;"></span><span class="mord">Δ</span><span class="mord mathnormal">κ</span><span class="mpunct">,</span></span></span></span></span>
<p data-start="2290" data-end="2361">with $\Delta \kappa$ the extrapolated curvature difference on overlaps.</p>
<hr data-start="2363" data-end="2366">
<p data-start="2368" data-end="2400">This categorical embedding says:</p>
<ul data-start="2402" data-end="2650">
<li data-start="2402" data-end="2462">
<p data-start="2404" data-end="2462"><strong data-start="2404" data-end="2433">Emotions = sheaf sections</strong> (local inoculation rules).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2463" data-end="2525">
<p data-start="2465" data-end="2525"><strong data-start="2465" data-end="2505">Mismatch = cohomological obstruction</strong> (rupture, grief).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2526" data-end="2583">
<p data-start="2528" data-end="2583"><strong data-start="2528" data-end="2567">Resolution = natural transformation</strong> (humor, joy).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="2584" data-end="2650">
<p data-start="2586" data-end="2650"><strong data-start="2586" data-end="2628">Recursive depth = morphism composition</strong> (fear, guilt, awe).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="2652" data-end="2655">
<p data-start="2657" data-end="2911" data-is-last-node="" data-is-only-node="">Would you like me to now expand this into a <strong data-start="2701" data-end="2719">worked example</strong> — e.g. humor as a natural transformation between two affective functors, with explicit diagrammatic commutativity? That would give a concrete mathematical illustration alongside the taxonomy.</p></div></div></div></div><div class="flex min-h-[46px] justify-start"><div class="touch:-me-2 touch:-ms-3.5 -ms-2.5 -me-1 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 p-1 select-none touch:w-[calc(100%+--spacing(3.5))] -mt-1 w-[calc(100%+--spacing(2.5))] duration-[1.5s] focus-within:transition-none hover:transition-none pointer-events-none [mask-image:linear-gradient(to_right,black_33%,transparent_66%)] [mask-size:300%_100%] [mask-position:100%_0%] motion-safe:transition-[mask-position] group-hover/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-hover/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] group-focus-within/turn-messages:pointer-events-auto group-focus-within/turn-messages:[mask-position:0_0] has-data-[state=open]:pointer-events-auto has-data-[state=open]:[mask-position:0_0]" style="mask-position: 0% 0%;"><button class="text-token-text-secondary hover:bg-token-bg-secondary rounded-lg" aria-label="Copy" aria-pressed="false" data-testid="copy-turn-action-button" data-state="closed"><span class="flex items-center justify-center touch:w-10 h-8 w-8"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="icon"><path d="M12.668 10.667C12.668 9.95614 12.668 9.46258 12.6367 9.0791C12.6137 8.79732 12.5758 8.60761 12.5244 8.46387L12.4688 8.33399C12.3148 8.03193 12.0803 7.77885 11.793 7.60254L11.666 7.53125C11.508 7.45087 11.2963 7.39395 10.9209 7.36328C10.5374 7.33197 10.0439 7.33203 9.33301 7.33203H6.5C5.78896 7.33203 5.29563 7.33195 4.91211 7.36328C4.63016 7.38632 4.44065 7.42413 4.29688 7.47559L4.16699 7.53125C3.86488 7.68518 3.61186 7.9196 3.43555 8.20703L3.36524 