d and reintegrate:</p>
<hr data-start="293" data-end="296">
<h3 data-start="298" data-end="321">1. <strong data-start="305" data-end="321">Introduction</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="322" data-end="805">
<li data-start="322" data-end="397">
<p data-start="324" data-end="397">Right now, it sets up the manifold hypothesis and extrapolated curvature.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="398" data-end="698">
<p data-start="400" data-end="470"><strong data-start="400" data-end="414">Expansion:</strong> Add a forward reference that the essay will also cover:</p>
<ul data-start="473" data-end="698">
<li data-start="473" data-end="539">
<p data-start="475" data-end="539">humor as manifold interference via frame-shift pattern matching,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="542" data-end="593">
<p data-start="544" data-end="593">a taxonomy of emotions via recursive inoculation,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="596" data-end="646">
<p data-start="598" data-end="646">developmental trajectories (ontogenetic parade),</p>
</li>
<li data-start="649" data-end="698">
<p data-start="651" data-end="698">empirical grounding in geometric hyperscanning.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-start="699" data-end="805">
<p data-start="701" data-end="805">This frames the essay as not just geometry + psychiatry, but a broader theory of affect and interaction.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="807" data-end="810">
<h3 data-start="812" data-end="866">2. <strong data-start="819" data-end="866">Semantic Manifolds / Extrapolated Curvature</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="867" data-end="1084">
<li data-start="867" data-end="900">
<p data-start="869" data-end="900">Currently formal and geometric.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="901" data-end="997">
<p data-start="903" data-end="997"><strong data-start="903" data-end="917">Expansion:</strong> Add worked emotional examples here (surprise spikes, separation anxiety model).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="998" data-end="1084">
<p data-start="1000" data-end="1084">Could also integrate the idea of learning = inoculation and play = simulated danger.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1086" data-end="1089">
<h3 data-start="1091" data-end="1125">3. <strong data-start="1098" data-end="1125">Geometric Hyperscanning</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="1126" data-end="1392">
<li data-start="1126" data-end="1142">
<p data-start="1128" data-end="1142">Already solid.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1143" data-end="1392">
<p data-start="1145" data-end="1224"><strong data-start="1145" data-end="1159">Expansion:</strong> Add a subsection “Ontogenetic Parade as Hyperscanning Baseline”:</p>
<ul data-start="1227" data-end="1392">
<li data-start="1227" data-end="1318">
<p data-start="1229" data-end="1318">argue that curvature–entropy spikes across ages mirror the developmental parade of fears,</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1321" data-end="1392">
<p data-start="1323" data-end="1392">link predictable “fear ridges” to age-dependent synchrony signatures.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start="1394" data-end="1397">
<h3 data-start="1399" data-end="1429">4. <strong data-start="1406" data-end="1429">Affective Inference</strong></h3>
<ul data-start="1430" data-end="1637">
<li data-start="1430" data-end="1471">
<p data-start="1432" data-end="1471">Right now about therapy and regulation.</p>
