<p data-start="409" data-end="420">This way:</p>
<ul data-start="421" data-end="585">
<li data-start="421" data-end="486">
<p data-start="423" data-end="486">You get a <strong data-start="433" data-end="468">standalone "Appendices" heading</strong> (not numbered).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="487" data-end="517">
<p data-start="489" data-end="517">It appears in the <strong data-start="507" data-end="514">TOC</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="518" data-end="585">
<p data-start="520" data-end="585">Each appendix still has its own numbered section (<code data-start="570" data-end="573">A</code>, <code data-start="575" data-end="578">B</code>, …).</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="587" data-end="725">If you instead want <em data-start="607" data-end="638">just one heading "Appendices"</em> and no separate A/B/C numbering, you can simply <strong data-start="687" data-end="711">not call <code data-start="698" data-end="709">\appendix</code></strong> and use only:</p>
